From c0a194f815cd75989ea2c1fb97494c7c0bfc824f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lovelace's Square <noreply@lovelacesquare.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:21:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Let assistants connect: a setting that opens every
 window's control channel

A window opened from the file manager has no control port, so an
assistant the user works with (an MCP client, say) cannot join the deck
the user is editing. Preferences gets an Assistants section with "Let
assistants connect to this window", off by default. When on, a window
started without --control opens its control channel as `--control auto`
does (a free port, the key file named after it); the key is still
required on every request. As in WordCraft.

- ui-egui: UiState::allow_assistants (allowAssistants in ui.json), the
  `app.allowAssistants {on?}` UI command (no value toggles, like the
  other switches) and the `allowAssistants` key of ui.set, and the
  checkbox with a short note in Preferences (not on the web, which has
  no control channel).
- deckcraft: the setting picks `auto` at start-up when no port was
  given; changed while running, it is saved at once (so windows opened
  next follow it) and turning it on opens this window's channel. Turning
  it off leaves an open channel until the window closes.
- docs: control-protocol.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
