@@ -25,6 +25,11 @@ writes a new key. `<settings>` is the folder that holds the preferences: on Linu
 Flatpak instance id inside Flatpak, and `local-<port>` otherwise, with the port the window is
 listening on (also with `auto`). On Unix the file has mode 0600.
 
+A window started without `--control` has no control channel, unless Preferences › Assistants ›
+Let assistants connect (`allowAssistants` in `ui.json`, off by default) is on: then it opens one as
+`--control auto` does. Turning it on also opens the current window's channel and saves the
+setting at once; turning it off leaves an open channel until the window closes.
+
 ```sh
 cat ~/.config/deckcraft/control-key.local-7979   # Linux, outside Flatpak, port 7979
 ```
